    {
      "n": 2,
      "title": "Lipids",
      "competency": "STEM_BIO11/12-II-i-j-15",
      "content": "<h3>🎯 Learning Objectives</h3><ul><li>Describe the structure of lipids.</li><li>Differentiate triglycerides, phospholipids, and steroids.</li><li>Explain the functions of lipids.</li><li>Relate lipid structure to function.</li></ul><h3>🔑 Key Concepts</h3><ul><li><strong>Lipid</strong> — hydrophobic biological molecule.</li><li><strong>Triglyceride</strong> — glycerol + 3 fatty acids (fat/oil).</li><li><strong>Phospholipid</strong> — glycerol + 2 fatty acids + phosphate group.</li><li><strong>Steroid</strong> — four fused rings (e.g., cholesterol, testosterone).</li></ul><h3>📚 Lesson Content</h3><h4>A. Types of Lipids</h4><table><thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Structure</th><th>Function</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Triglyceride</td><td>Glycerol + 3 fatty acids</td><td>Energy storage, insulation</td></tr><tr><td>Phospholipid</td><td>Glycerol + 2 fatty acids + phosphate</td><td>Cell membranes</td></tr><tr><td>Steroid</td><td>Four fused rings</td><td>Hormones, cholesterol</td></tr></tbody></table><h4>B. Saturated vs Unsaturated Fats</h4><ul><li><strong>Saturated</strong> — no double bonds; solid at room temperature (butter)</li><li><strong>Unsaturated</strong> — one or more double bonds; liquid at room temperature (olive oil)</li></ul><h4>C. Functions in Metabolism</h4><ul><li>Long-term energy storage</li><li>Structural component of membranes</li><li>Hormone synthesis (steroids)</li><li>Thermal insulation</li></ul>",
      "activity1": {
        "timeLimit": 90,
        "badgeId": "lipid-master",
        "badgeName": "Lipid Master",
        "badgeIcon": "🧈",
        "pairs": [
          { "key": "tri", "left": "Triglyceride", "right": "Glycerol + 3 fatty acids" },
          { "key": "phos", "left": "Phospholipid", "right": "Glycerol + 2 fatty acids + phosphate" },
          { "key": "ster", "left": "Steroid", "right": "Four fused rings" },
          { "key": "sat", "left": "Saturated fat", "right": "Solid at room temp" },
          { "key": "unsat", "left": "Unsaturated fat", "right": "Liquid at room temp" },
          { "key": "chol", "left": "Cholesterol", "right": "Membrane fluidity + steroid precursor" }
        ]
      },
      "activity2": {
        "timePerCard": 12,
        "badgeId": "lipid-detective",
