    {
      "n": 4,
      "title": "Nucleic Acids & Roles in Metabolism",
      "competency": "STEM_BIO11/12-II-i-j-15, -16",
      "content": "<h3>🎯 Learning Objectives</h3><ul><li>Describe the structure of nucleic acids.</li><li>Differentiate DNA from RNA.</li><li>Explain the roles of biological molecules in metabolism.</li><li>Summarize the four biomolecules.</li></ul><h3>🔑 Key Concepts</h3><ul><li><strong>Nucleotide</strong> — monomer of nucleic acids (sugar + phosphate + base).</li><li><strong>DNA</strong> — deoxyribonucleic acid; stores genetic info.</li><li><strong>RNA</strong> — ribonucleic acid; transmits genetic info.</li><li><strong>ATP</strong> — energy currency of the cell.</li></ul><h3>📚 Lesson Content</h3><h4>A. Nucleotide Structure</h4><p>Each nucleotide has: a pentose sugar, a phosphate group, and a nitrogenous base.</p><h4>B. DNA vs RNA</h4><table><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>DNA</th><th>RNA</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Sugar</td><td>Deoxyribose</td><td>Ribose</td></tr><tr><td>Strands</td><td>Double helix</td><td>Single strand</td></tr><tr><td>Bases</td><td>A, T, G, C</td><td>A, U, G, C</td></tr><tr><td>Function</td><td>Genetic storage</td><td>Protein synthesis</td></tr></tbody></table><h4>C. Roles in Metabolism</h4><ul><li><strong>Carbohydrates:</strong> quick energy (ATP)</li><li><strong>Lipids:</strong> long-term energy & membranes</li><li><strong>Proteins:</strong> enzymes catalyze reactions</li><li><strong>Nucleic acids:</strong> store and transmit genetic info</li></ul>",
      "activity1": {
